.TH "dotnet-project-convert" "1" "2026-04-30" "" ".NET Documentation"
.hy
.SH dotnet project convert
.PP
\f[B]This article applies to:\f[R] \[u2714]\[uFE0F] .NET 10 SDK and later versions
.SH NAME
.PP
dotnet-project-convert - Converts a file-based program to a project-based program.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
dotnet project convert <FILE> [--dry-run] [--force] [--interactive]
    [-o|--output <OUTPUT_DIRECTORY>]

dotnet project convert -h|--help
\f[R]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The \f[V]dotnet project convert\f[R] command converts a file-based program to a project-based program.
This command creates a new directory named for your file, scaffolds a \f[I].csproj\f[R] file, moves your code into a file with the same name as the input file, and translates any \f[V]#:\f[R] directives into MSBuild properties and references.
.PP
This makes the transition seamless, from a single file to a fully functional, buildable, and extensible project.
When your file-based app grows in complexity, or you simply want the extra capabilities afforded in project-based apps, you can convert it to a standard project.
.SS Conversion process
.PP
The command performs the following operations:
.IP "1." 3
Creates a new directory named after the input file (without extension).
.IP "2." 3
Generates a \f[I].csproj\f[R] file with appropriate SDK and properties.
.IP "3." 3
Moves the source code to a file with the same name as the input file.
.IP "4." 3
Removes \f[V]#:\f[R] directives from the source code.
.IP "5." 3
Translates \f[V]#:sdk\f[R] directives: the first \f[V]#:sdk\f[R] directive becomes the \f[V]<Project Sdk=\[dq]Sdk.Id\[dq]>\f[R] or \f[V]<Project Sdk=\[dq]Sdk.Id/version\[dq]>\f[R] attribute, and any additional \f[V]#:sdk\f[R] directives become \f[V]<Sdk Name=\[dq]Sdk.Id\[dq] />\f[R] or \f[V]<Sdk Name=\[dq]Sdk.Id\[dq] Version=\[dq]version\[dq] />\f[R] elements.
.IP "6." 3
Translates \f[V]#:package\f[R] directives to \f[V]<PackageReference>\f[R] elements in the project file.
.IP "7." 3
Translates \f[V]#:property\f[R] directives to MSBuild properties in the project file.
.IP "8." 3
Sets appropriate MSBuild properties based on the SDK and framework detected.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[V]FILE\f[R]
.RS 2
.PP
The path to the file-based program to convert.
The file must be a C# source file (typically with a \f[I].cs\f[R] extension).
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]\f[VB]--dry-run\f[B]\f[R]
.RS 2
.PP
Determines changes without actually modifying the file system.
Shows what would be created or modified without performing the conversion.
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]\f[VB]--force\f[B]\f[R]
.RS 2
.PP
Forces conversion even if there are malformed directives.
By default, the command fails if it encounters directives that cannot be properly parsed or converted.
.RE
.PP
\f[B]\f[VB]--interactive\f[B]\f[R]
.PP
Allows the command to stop and wait for user input or action.
For example, to complete authentication.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]\f[VB]-o|--output <OUTPUT_DIRECTORY>\f[B]\f[R]
.RS 2
.PP
Specifies the output directory for the converted project.
If not specified, a directory is created with the same name as the input file (without extension) in the current directory.
.RE
.PP
\f[B]\f[VB]-?|-h|--help\f[B]\f[R]
.PP
Prints out a description of how to use the command.
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP \[bu] 2
Convert a file-based program to a project:
.RS 2
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
dotnet project convert app.cs
\f[R]
.fi
.PP
Given a folder containing \f[I]app.cs\f[R] with the following content:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
#:sdk Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Web
#:package Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi\[at]10.*-*

var builder = WebApplication.CreateBuilder();

builder.Services.AddOpenApi();

var app = builder.Build();

app.MapGet(\[dq]/\[dq], () => \[dq]Hello, world!\[dq]);
app.Run();
\f[R]
.fi
.PP
Running \f[V]dotnet project convert app.cs\f[R] results in a folder called \f[I]app\f[R] containing:
.PP
\f[I]app/app.cs\f[R]:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
var builder = WebApplication.CreateBuilder();

builder.Services.AddOpenApi();

var app = builder.Build();

app.MapGet(\[dq]/\[dq], () => \[dq]Hello, world!\[dq]);
app.Run();
\f[R]
.fi
.PP
\f[I]app/app.csproj\f[R]:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
<Project Sdk=\[dq]Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Web\[dq]>

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <PublishAot>true</PublishAot>
    <PackAsTool>true</PackAsTool>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include=\[dq]Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi\[dq] Version=\[dq]10.*-*\[dq] />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
\f[R]
.fi
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
Convert a file-based program to a project in a specific output directory:
.RS 2
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
dotnet project convert app.cs --output MyProject
\f[R]
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \[bu] 2
dotnet build
.IP \[bu] 2
dotnet run
.IP \[bu] 2
dotnet publish
.IP \[bu] 2
